  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "When counting from \\(3\\) to \\(201,\\) the number \\(53\\) is in position \\(51.\\) When counting backward from \\(201\\) to \\(3,\\) the number \\(53\\) is in position \\(n.\\) What is \\(n?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 146 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 147 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 148 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 149 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 150 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Counting backward from \\(201\\) to \\(53\\) requires \\(201-53=148\\) decreases by \\(1\\). The starting number \\(201\\) already occupies position \\(1\\), so the position of \\(53\\) is\n\\[\nn=148+1=\\boxed{149}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\text{D}\\).",
